                <pb facs="0630" n="508" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg508"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr.
                            Preston.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-12-10"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 10,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your telegram received. The American minister at Port au Prince has been fully
                    instructed to inform the provisional authorities there of the President’s
                    decision in the case of the <hi rendition="#italic">Haytien Republic</hi>, so
                    that nothing more will be necessary than compliance with that decision.</p>
                <p>The U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Galena</hi> will sail from New York
                    to-morrow morning, and should you desire to avail yourself of the courtesy, the
                    commander will no doubt convey your communications.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
